{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123947","id":4671907915,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFneoSw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123947","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123947.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123947.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123947","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123947/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123947/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123947/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/93266de8f995b30111989286264aade0432f46ea","number":123947,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"macOS: Use blocking frame delays in headless mode","user":{"login":"KevinZonda","id":33132228,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMyMjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33132228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda","html_url":"https://github.com/KevinZonda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The headless main loop polls CFRunLoop without waiting. When the macOS frame delay uses an asynchronous timer, such as while Magnet is running, the loop keeps iterating and resetting the timer instead of sleeping. Repeated application lookups can also keep `launchservicesd` busy.\r\n\r\nOverride the headless frame delay to use the existing blocking Unix implementation, preserving frame caps and the default headless sleep.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nOn macOS, a headless Godot process can busy-loop and cause high `launchservicesd` CPU usage while Magnet is running, even with `Engine.max_fps` set.\r\n\r\n`OS_MacOS::add_frame_delay()` queries whether Magnet is running and, when it is, schedules a CFRunLoop timer instead of blocking. However, `OS_MacOS_Headless::run()` only polls the run loop with `CFRunLoopRunInMode(..., 0, 0)`. It does not wait for the frame timer, so it repeatedly advances frames, replaces the timer, and queries Launch Services.\r\n\r\nOverride `add_frame_delay()` in `OS_MacOS_Headless` to call the existing blocking `OS_Unix::add_frame_delay()`. This preserves frame caps and the default headless sleep while avoiding the AppKit timer and Magnet lookup path. The windowed and embedded implementations are unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n\r\nReproduced on 4.8-dev branch at `941ea1816d654e4ffeac10a260d64a8555890cf6` and on 4.7.2 (stable). Tested on macOS 14.8.7, Apple M2, with Magnet 3.0.7 running throughout.\r\n\r\n### Validation\r\n\r\nThe same empty-project probe runs for three seconds of real time, with an external timeout that terminates and reaps stalled children. Before/after builds use the same configuration; only this patch differs.\r\n\r\n| Configuration | Before: iterations/s | After: iterations/s | Before: launchservicesd CPU | After: launchservicesd CPU |\r\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\r\n| `--headless`, 120 FPS | 17,582.7 | 121.0 | 55.55% | 0.26% |\r\n| `--headless`, 60 FPS | 19,941.5 | 60.7 | 67.05% | 0.32% |\r\n| `--headless`, default cap 0 | 19,060.0 | 145.9 | 65.22% | 0.32% |\r\n| `--display-driver headless`, 120 FPS | 20,094.1 | 121.0 | 65.52% | 0.32% |\r\n\r\nThese are main-loop iterations, not rendered frames. With cap 0, the normal 6900 µs headless sleep gives roughly 145 iterations/s. The short probe includes startup effects. CPU values use the daemon's accumulated CPU time over process wall time and may include unrelated clients.\r\n\r\n- All four patched runs exited successfully with no script errors or timeouts.\r\n- Local arm64 `template_debug` build passed.\r\n- `clang-format` 22.1.5 and `git diff --check` passed.\r\n- A sample of the unpatched process spent most main-thread samples in `NSRunningApplication.runningApplicationsWithBundleIdentifier:` and Launch Services synchronous IPC.\r\n\r\n### Minimal reproduction\r\n\r\nWith Magnet running on macOS, save the following as `reproduce.gd` in an empty Godot project and run:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n/path/to/godot --headless --path . --script res://reproduce.gd\r\n```\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends SceneTree\r\n\r\nvar started_usec: int\r\nvar iterations := 0\r\n\r\nfunc _initialize() -> void:\r\n\tEngine.max_fps = 120\r\n\tstarted_usec = Time.get_ticks_usec()\r\n\r\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> bool:\r\n\titerations += 1\r\n\tvar elapsed := (Time.get_ticks_usec() - started_usec) / 1000000.0\r\n\tif elapsed < 3.0:\r\n\t\treturn false\r\n\tprint(\"iterations/s=\", iterations / elapsed, \", max_fps=\", Engine.max_fps)\r\n\treturn true\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe script exits after approximately three seconds. Affected builds report thousands of iterations/s; the patched build reports approximately 120. Use an editor binary or first import the empty project when testing a template-only build.\r\n\r\n### AI disclosure\r\n\r\nThis bug is firstly found in my (KevinZonda) project and got investigation under Codex's help.\r\n\r\nThe patch was authored by an autonomous AI agent (OpenAI Codex + GPT 6 Astra xhigh), and was fully reviewed by KevinZonda (me, a human), to diagnose and fix macOS headless frame pacing. The agent inspected the source, implemented the patch, compiled both versions and ran the local before/after check. KevinZonda fully reviewed the patched code and did the qualitative validation.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-29T02:54:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T03:09:41Z","closed_at":"2026-09-29T03:09:30Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e08d66736d684525a8ad8c0e15aff3af12d6366b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"KevinZonda:fix-macos-headless-frame-delay","ref":"fix-macos-headless-frame-delay","repo":{"id":1394109234,"node_id":"R_kgDOUxhrMg","name":"godot","full_name":"KevinZonda/godot","owner":{"login":"KevinZonda","id":33132228,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMTMyMjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33132228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KevinZonda","html_url":"https://github.com/KevinZonda","followers_url":"https://api.git